   "text": {
    "L1": "Division makes equal groups. It can mean sharing or grouping.",
    "L2": "Sharing asks, “How many does each get?” Grouping asks, “How many groups can we make?”",
    "L3": "Both meanings use the same division idea, but the question changes.",
    "L4": "Every division matches a multiplication. For example, 48 divided by 6 is 8 because 6 times 8 is 48.",
    "L5": "Let us share 27 pencils among 4 children. The biggest 4-table number not over 27 is 4 times 6, or 24.",
    "L6": "Each child gets 6 pencils, and 3 pencils are left. The leftover is smaller than 4, so there is no more full group.",
    "L7": "A remainder cannot be as big as the group size. If it were 4 or more, another group could be made.",
    "L8": "Now choose the correct result for 23 divided by 4. The host will check your choice."
   },
